":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-25T23:46:01Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T18:41:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6.1, 4.7.dev\n\n### System information\n\nForward+, D3D12\n\n### Issue description\n\nwhat the title says. The light source is not being added to `p_instance->scenario->dynamic_lights`. Thus, it is ignored in SDFGI, until you toggle its visibility off and on again. Also seems to happen when you first load the scene.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the editor, add an OmniLight3D to a scene. \n\n(Optional) In `servers\\rendering\\renderer_scene_cull.cpp`, add breakpoint inside the if body at:\n```\n\t\t\tif (p_instance->visible && p_instance->scenario && light->bake_mode == RS::LIGHT_BAKE_DYNAMIC) {\n\t\t\t\tp_instance->scenario->dynamic_lights.push_back(light->instance);\n\t\t\t}\n```\nDuplicate the light source.\nObserve that the breakpoint is not hit and the new light source is ignored in SDFGI.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\ntrivial.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116780/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116780/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}